Subject: [PATCH] device: raise the A2DP ACL priority on Broadcom controllers

The TempoTec V1 firmware ships a BlueZ 5.54 with a vendor patch that, once the
A2DP sink service of a device is connected, sends the Broadcom vendor command
0xfd1a (set ACL priority: connection handle, 0x01, 0x00) on a raw HCI socket, so
the AP6212 keeps the audio link going while Wi-Fi shares the radio. Port the
same behaviour behind a main.conf option, [General] BroadcomHighPriority
(default false). It only acts on Broadcom/Cypress controllers (manufacturer
from the HCI version information) and ignores every failure.

